# Reduce rules mapping an all-atom protein onto Martini 3.0.0 coarse-grain
# beads. Generated by data/martini3/prepare_martini3_data.py -- do not edit
# by hand. Pair it with forcefield/martini3.nbi.ff, which declares every
# grain name this file produces, terminal qualifiers included.
#
# Unlike data/martini/reducerules/martini.grp, this is a REAL reduction: it
# takes an atomic structure and builds the beads itself, so martinize is not
# in the pipeline. Atom names are AMBER's.
#
# HEAVY ATOMS ONLY, AND THAT IS THE ACCURATE CHOICE, not a shortcut. A
# Martini bead is the MASS-weighted average of its atoms (martinize2 runs
# vermouth's DoAverageBead with center_weight = "mass"); a BioSpring grain is
# measure::centroid, an unweighted mean. Over the 401 beads of
# example/001_GKinase/model.pdb, listing the heavy atoms only lands 0.028 A
# from the true Martini bead in the median and 0.415 A at worst, where
# listing Martini's weight-1 atoms with their hydrogens lands 0.342 A and
# 0.730 A -- twelve times further, because an unweighted centroid gives a
# hydrogen the same pull as a carbon and a mass-weighted one gives it 1/13 of
# that. The worst residual is on the sulfur beads: CYS SC1 is CB at 12 Da and
# SG at 32.
#
# The input therefore does NOT need hydrogens. Any it has are claimed by no
# rule and reported one per atom, which is correct and expected -- they are
# not part of any bead here.
#
# A free chain end gets its own ":NTER"/":CTER" rules, which REPLACE the
# unqualified ones rather than adding to them, and its own force-field keys
# so that it carries Martini's terminal charge. Their atom lists differ from
# the interior one only by OXT at the C end, the N end having no heavy atom
# of its own.
#
#
# --- Interior residues ---
ABB ALA N CA C O
ASC1 ALA CB
CBB CYS N CA C O
CSC1 CYS CB SG
DBB ASP N CA C O
DSC1 ASP CB CG OD1 OD2
DHBB ASH N CA C O
DHSC1 ASH CB CG OD1 OD2
EBB GLU N CA C O
ESC1 GLU CB CG CD OE1 OE2
EHBB GLH N CA C O
EHSC1 GLH CB CG CD OE1 OE2
FBB PHE N CA C O
FSC1 PHE CB CG CD1
FSC2 PHE CE1
FSC3 PHE CZ CD2 CE2
GBB GLY N CA C O
HBB HIS N CA C O
HSC1 HIS CB CG
HSC2 HIS CD2 NE2
HSC3 HIS ND1 CE1
HEBB HIE N CA C O
HESC1 HIE CB CG
HESC2 HIE CD2 NE2
HESC3 HIE ND1 CE1
HPBB HIP N CA C O
HPSC1 HIP CB CG
HPSC2 HIP CD2 NE2
HPSC3 HIP ND1 CE1
IBB ILE N CA C O
ISC1 ILE CB CG1 CG2 CD1
KBB LYS N CA C O
KSC1 LYS CB CG CD
KSC2 LYS CE NZ
KNBB LYN N CA C O
KNSC1 LYN CB CG CD
KNSC2 LYN CE NZ
LBB LEU N CA C O
LSC1 LEU CB CG CD1 CD2
MBB MET N CA C O
MSC1 MET CB CG SD CE
NBB ASN N CA C O
NSC1 ASN CB CG OD1 ND2
OBB HYP N CA C O
OSC1 HYP CB CG CD OD1
PBB PRO N CA C O
PSC1 PRO CB CG CD
QBB GLN N CA C O
QSC1 GLN CB CG CD OE1 NE2
RBB ARG N CA C O
RSC1 ARG CB CG CD
RSC2 ARG NE CZ NH1 NH2
SBB SER N CA C O
SSC1 SER CB OG
TBB THR N CA C O
TSC1 THR CB OG1 CG2
VBB VAL N CA C O
VSC1 VAL CB CG1 CG2
WBB TRP N CA C O
WSC1 TRP CB CG
WSC2 TRP CD1 NE1
WSC3 TRP CE2 CD2
WSC4 TRP CE3 CZ3
WSC5 TRP CZ2 CH2
YBB TYR N CA C O
YSC1 TYR CB CG
YSC2 TYR CD1 CE1
YSC3 TYR CD2 CE2
YSC4 TYR CZ OH
#
# --- Free N-terminus ---
ABB ALA:NTER N CA C O
ASC1 ALA:NTER CB
CBB CYS:NTER N CA C O
CSC1 CYS:NTER CB SG
DBB ASP:NTER N CA C O
DSC1 ASP:NTER CB CG OD1 OD2
